# The files under this directory are evidence, not source: every manifest records the sha256 of the
# exact bytes it copied.  This host writes the live ST-6 artefacts with CRLF line endings and git's
# text conversion (core.autocrlf=true here) would rewrite them on the way into the object store, so
# the recorded digest would describe bytes no reader could reproduce from the commit — the snapshot
# would reproduce only on the machine that took it.  `-text` disables the conversion for everything
# below, and the copies are then stored verbatim.
* -text
